 a single need, so **is** links it to time.","C":"The complement is uncountable time and the clause presents one need, so plural are does not fit this example.","D":"Be is not a finite present form."}}},{"id":"8245ad12-b69f-59af-abeb-5834129cb15f","topicSlug":"clefts-emphasis","level":"C1","prompt":"Correct the claim that she never does the task: “She does ____ the garden fence!”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"measures"},{"id":"B","text":"measured"},{"id":"C","text":"to measure"},{"id":"D","text":"measure"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Emphasis adds **does**, which takes over the agreement marking.","explanation":"Emphatic **does** carries the agreement, so choose base **measure**.","keywords":["emphatic-present"],"skill":"emphatic-present","contextKey":"clefts-emphasis-3","fingerprint":"7a2c672fed701abcf5eaddf595acf072dc44abf6e15773bcab1f419d7309e3f1","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-emphasis"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Emphasis adds **does**, which takes over the agreement marking.","Emphatic **does** carries the agreement, so choose base **measure**.","Choose **measure**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The -s agreement is already on does.","B":"Does is present; the following verb still needs base form.","C":"Emphatic do takes a bare infinitive.","D":"Emphatic **does** carries the agreement, so choose base **measure**."}}},{"id":"ba7e861e-aebc-5488-a64b-9813daa58148","topicSlug":"clefts-emphasis","level":"C1","prompt":"Correct a denial about yesterday: “We did ____ the garden fence!”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"measure"},{"id":"B","text":"measured"},{"id":"C","text":"measures"},{"id":"D","text":"to measure"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The auxiliary carries both **past tense and emphasis**.","explanation":"Emphatic **did** carries the past tense, so use **measure**.","keywords":["emphatic-past"],"skill":"emphatic-past","contextKey":"clefts-emphasis-3","fingerprint":"0e3a09c1f9a95300131caa1a9c403faa7869799e3520dacc6da272056beea3f1","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-emphasis"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The auxiliary carries both **past tense and emphasis**.","Emphatic **did** carries the past tense, so use **measure**.","Choose **measure**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Emphatic **did** carries the past tense, so use **measure**.","B":"The past marker is already on did.","C":"A third-person present form cannot follow did.","D":"Did takes a bare infinitive."}}},{"id":"6f4931df-5420-5bba-a537-9185e764248a","topicSlug":"clefts-emphasis","level":"C1","prompt":"Focus on the person: “It was the assistant ____ measured the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"who"},{"id":"B","text":"whose"},{"id":"C","text":"where"},{"id":"D","text":"what"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The focused element is a **person**, and the following clause needs its subject.","explanation":"**Who** links the focused person to the action in this it-cleft.","keywords":["person-cleft"],"skill":"person-cleft","contextKey":"clefts-emphasis-3","fingerprint":"6e61a95d03871d286ee6fd72af576a299250cca09a67f5007e7d1ee4f7dc158a","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-emphasis"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The focused element is a **person**, and the following clause needs its subject.","**Who** links the focused person to the action in this it-cleft.","Choose **who**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**Who** links the focused person to the action in this it-cleft.","B":"Whose would need a noun after it to mark possession.","C":"Where does not represent the person performing this action.","D":"What does not normally follow a named person as the cleft connector here."}}},{"id":"43973d82-49ea-5c3c-a630-bd83c5c4dce6","topicSlug":"clefts-emphasis","level":"C1","prompt":"Complete the what-cleft: “What I need ____ time to measure the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"am"},{"id":"B","text":"is"},{"id":"C","text":"are"},{"id":"D","text":"be"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"The subject is the whole **what I need** clause, not the I inside it.","explanation":"The what-clause presents a single need, so **is** links it to time.","keywords":["what-cleft-agreement"],"skill":"what-cleft-agreement","contextKey":"clefts-emphasis-3","fingerprint":"5c0f67b84a8625390e0092851a5901bba0189bdfc9a987bba2840308d6bb9722","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-emphasis"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The subject is the whole **what I need** clause, not the I inside it.","The what-clause presents a single need, so **is** links it to time.","Choose **is**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Am agrees with I as a main subject, not with the whole what-clause.","B":"The what-clause presents a single need, so **is** links it to time.","C":"The complement is uncountable time and the clause presents one need, so plural are does not fit this example.","D":"Be is not a finite present form."}}},{"id":"e46ef891-9e92-5e83-a36c-d2d4c486f352","topicSlug":"clefts-emphasis","level":"C1","prompt":"Correct the claim that she never does the task: “She does ____ the travel leaflet!”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"translated"},{"id":"B","text":"to translate"},{"id":"C","text":"translate"},{"id":"D","text":"translates"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Emphasis adds **does**, which 